&lt;h1&gt;About Co-Star&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Someone downloads Co–Star every 5 seconds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the five years since we launched, 25% of young people 18-25 in the US have downloaded the app. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dAl8qGIrcSI&amp;amp;t=203s&quot;&gt;Big Sean&lt;/a&gt; has rapped about us, Ariana Grande &amp;amp; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.12up.com/posts/kevin-durant-posts-cryptic-instagram-story-amid-free-agency-and-injury-rumors-01dcsry062kv&quot;&gt;Kevin Durant&lt;/a&gt; post screenshots to their IGs, and we’ve been &lt;a href=&quot;https://apps.apple.com/us/story/id1458814851&quot;&gt;App of the Day&lt;/a&gt; twice. We’ve been featured in the New York Times three times, this year on the cover of &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/04/style/astrology-co-star-ai.html&quot;&gt;NYT Style&lt;/a&gt;. We have a global following, in 193 countries – missing just North Korea and Eritrea.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t pay for marketing – we designed the app to go viral, and it did.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Astrology has been popular for 4,000 years.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Astrology is a tool for speaking about yourself, about who you are, what you’re experiencing, and how you relate to other people – in other words, a language for the things that really matter. It’s a structured system, based on the physical locations of the planets in the sky, developed over millennia 4,000 years of practice.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everyone has memories of reading a horoscope in the newspaper. You know your sign the same way you know the name of the street you grew up on. &lt;a href=&quot;https://ncses.nsf.gov/pubs/nsb20207/data#supplemental-tables&quot;&gt;An average of 43% of Americans have believed in astrology since the 1970s.&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;We’re merging the resonance of the humanities with the precision of technology.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Co-Star uses real-time NASA data and AI to bring this practice to the modern age. Every day, Co–Star generates millions of hyper-personalized horoscopes –&amp;nbsp;a scale never previously possible. Every word of it is based on each person’s unique astrology: where the stars physically were when they were born and where those same stars are now. Co–Star combines the art of ancient practice with cutting-edge artificial intelligence, creating the first synthetic text to be called “wildly beautiful.”&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;We’re a small, experienced team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Co-Star is a team of 30, with experience in big tech (Amazon, Google, Snapchat), entertainment (Frank Ocean, Adult Swim), and academia (Harvard, Stanford, NYU, Columbia).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;About the brand designer role&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a talented visual designer to shape how Co-Star shows up outside of the app, in the broader world. We are looking for someone with a fresh, opinionated, and high-quality design foundation who can create work that feels distinct, not what’s now but what’s next.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with the leadership on campaigns and visual storytelling across earned and owned channels. This is a freelance engagement with potential for a long-term partnership as the work (and team) grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design campaign visuals: ads, social, launches — from concept through finished assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring editorial design sensibility to our owned channels: email/welcome series, blog, campaign imagery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop visual systems that are expressive rather than corporate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with marketing on what earned and owned should look and feel like&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate async with a small, fast-moving team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You might be a fit if&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a senior IC — roughly 5–8 years in — with a portfolio of expressive, culturally fluent graphic design: editorial, campaigns, identities across print and digital&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Typography and composition are your first language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can direct as well as execute: you&#39;ve shaped campaigns, not just produced assets for them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re plugged into visual culture across art, fashion, publishing, music, and the internet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work well remotely and independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Editorial/publication experience (print or digital magazines)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motion or illustration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You already make things with generative tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Logistics&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Freelance/contract, part-time to start, with room to grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully remote, anywhere. No travel required (though you&#39;re always welcome in NYC)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;To apply&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Send your portfolio. We care about taste, range, and point of view.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;+++&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re expanding rapidly, so if you don&#39;t see a role that fits your expertise now, you can submit your resume here and include a brief note on how your background and experience would add value to Co-Star.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When we open a role that matches your experience, our recruiting team will reach out.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;While we respond to all people who apply through defined open roles, applications through this link may not receive a response. If there is an open job you&#39;re interested in, apply directly to that role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;+++&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the late 1960s, Bell Labs was grappling with a large project: an unwieldy operating system called Multics. It was too complex, too slow, and ultimately Bell withdrew. A small group of researchers, led by Ken Thompson and Dennis Ritchie, decided to start over—not with grand designs, but with simplicity at the core.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;They aimed for function over perfection and were deliberate in their collaboration. Engineers shared ideas as rough drafts, circulated them early, and refined them through iteration.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From this came Unix. It wasn&#39;t about working harder or sacrificing more - it was about getting ideas out quickly and leveraging collective intelligence early in the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is central to how we build at Co–Star: we start with simple solutions, share them early as written docs, and evolve them through real-world feedback.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Co–Star you’ll help tens of millions of people connect with each other and themselves—through astrology—in real, meaningful ways. We’re looking for a backend engineer who values feedback, who is both fast and deliberate, and who creates systems that let small teams deliver outsized results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product, design, and other engineers to deliver high-quality solutions that align with business priorities. You&#39;ll be a true collaborator who helps move the team forward as a unit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Break down complex problems to provide insight, technical guidance, and shape scope. You’ll weigh tradeoffs to find the best solution for the business and articulate those points in writing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own delivery and move quickly. We’re looking for someone who eagerly seeks feedback and actively moves the ball forward - who genuinely enjoys getting their code into the world.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-7 years of backend development experience. Knowledge of or excitement to learn Haskell.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love good documentation and testing. You know well-documented, tested code sets your future-self up for success.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sense of ownership over work end-to-end, accountability for results, and supportiveness for your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re passionate and pragmatic when problem solving. You focus on outcomes and enjoy solving user problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment. You can articulate tradeoffs clearly, especially when working with incomplete information or in pre-decision situations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You make informed decisions that balance speed with quality and see around corners to anticipate potential challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud infrastructure (AWS) and databases (we use PostgreSQL).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What we offer&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully covered $0 deductible healthcare + vision, dental, and therapy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) + 5% matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited vacation + 2 week company-wide recharge at the end of each year&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equipment budget&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12 weeks 100% paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Readings with in-house astrologers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A competitive total rewards package, including base salary, equity (stock options), and benefits. Our salary and equity ranges are highly competitive within the tech industry and are regularly updated using the most reliable compensation survey data. Offers are crafted based on a candidate’s experience, expertise, location, and internal equity relative to peers. Our target new hire base salary ranges for this role is $159,000-$205,000.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Co–Star is looking for an Operations and Customer Service Associate to take care of our users and our SoHo office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be the person behind the scenes making sure things work as they should. You’ll answer questions from the millions of people who use Co–Star, identify problems before they become patterns, and help translate what we hear from users back to the team. You’ll also keep our office stocked, organized, and running beautifully, and help bring Co–Star events to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a junior role for someone with good taste, excellent instincts, and a habit of noticing what needs to happen before anyone asks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage customer support through Zendesk, helping users with accounts, purchases, natal charts, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve macros and automated responses so support feels efficient without feeling impersonal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring issues, escalate edge cases, and share useful patterns with the product team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools and Claude Code regularly to automate repetitive work, analyze support data, and make our customer experience workflows more efficient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Co–Star events and daily office operations, from coordinating with vendors and creating a welcoming office environment to managing office equipment and ordering daily lunch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Notice what needs to be done, take ownership, and follow it through without waiting to be asked for a wide variety of tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You might be a fit if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You write clearly, warmly, and like a person.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re observant, organized, and unusually good at following through: you naturally anticipate what people will need and take care of it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong judgment and know when to solve something yourself and when to escalate it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You already use AI tools in your work and are excited to use Claude Code, even if you don’t consider yourself a programmer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience in customer support, hospitality, events, retail, or office operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-time in New York City. You’ll work from our SoHo office daily.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation: $65,000-83,000, plus benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;Product Designer&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the 1960s, the Italian artist and inventor Bruno Munari was studying spontaneous forms: shapes that emerge from the interaction of material, function, and environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When Danese Milano commissioned him to design a lamp that was practical, durable, affordable, and easy to transport, Munari was reminded of the traditional rice paper lanterns he had encountered when traveling in Japan. But rice paper lanterns are fragile, hard to clean, and tend to yellow over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Looking for an industrial alternative, he discovered filanca—a synthetic stretch nylon used exclusively for women&#39;s stockings at the time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Munari visited hosiery factories to test the material and see what forms it could take. &quot;We do not make lamps, sir. Only stockings,&quot; one factory told him. Munari replied, &quot;You&#39;ll see.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The result was the Falkland lamp: only a few centimeters thick when packaged, as tall as a human when hung, its spontaneous form emerging from the elasticity of the nylon and metal rings of different diameters inserted at regular intervals, enlarged by gravity when suspended from above.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Munari didn&#39;t begin with the form of a lamp. He began with the qualities it needed, then looked outside the conventions of lighting to find the right materials and methods. We&#39;re looking for a designer who works the same way: someone who studies the systems and materials at hand, then finds a way of putting them together that feels both unexpected and inevitable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Co–Star, the materials are a 4,000-year-old system of astrology, planetary data from NASA, and a corpus written by astrologers and poets. The qualities we&#39;re designing for: astrology made accessible without asking anyone to learn a complex system, and a language that lets people share something intimate with their friends.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Senior Product Designer to continue cultivating those qualities across Co–Star and new experiments. You&#39;ll move between product architecture, interaction design, prototyping, and visual design. Ideas rarely arrive as polished specs. You&#39;ll help decide what we make next and how it works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build products from concept through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with design and engineering on new features and launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care about the details—typography, layout, motion, responsiveness, loading states, and performance—that make an experience great.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute visual assets for marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype ideas quickly using Figma, Claude, Cursor, and whatever tools helps move the work forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You might be a fit if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 2–5 years of experience designing and building for the web.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You move fluidly across the full design process, from early concept through final production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an instinct for the details that make interfaces feel considered: type, spacing, motion, and how they all work together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know enough HTML and CSS to work effectively with engineers—or to build parts of the experience yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable using tools like Claude Code and Cursor as part of your workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;d rather prototype than make a presentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work &amp;gt; ego&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Logistics&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid in San Francisco or New York.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation: $150,500–$185,000 + benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;To apply&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A portfolio is required. We care much more about what you&#39;ve made than where you&#39;ve worked; if this sounds like you, apply even if you don&#39;t check every box.&lt;/p&gt;

