&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own major product surfaces end-to-end: concept, flows, interaction, visual polish, ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Invent interaction paradigms for things that haven&#39;t existed before and moke those new paradigms legible and fun&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use research, experimentation, analytics, and user feedback to understand what people need and where products can improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype constantly, in Figma and in code — we expect tools like Claude Code, Cursor, and v0 to be part of your workflow&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with engineering and research, to refine interactions, iterate quickly, and ship high-quality work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You might be a fit if:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve spent the last decade designing software people love to use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable moving between interaction design, visual design, and product thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy working closely with engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You agree that good work often emerges out of many rounds of iteration. You explore wildly, always ready to kill your darlings, and rework ideas until something clicks and feels correct.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;d rather prototype than make a presentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work &amp;gt; ego&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Logistics&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-time. Hybrid San Francisco or New York.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation: $200,000–$285,000 + benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;To apply&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A portfolio is required. We care much more about what you&#39;ve made than where you&#39;ve worked; if this sounds like you, apply even if you don&#39;t check every box.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Co–Star is hiring a Product Manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most of the products we build don’t have obvious precedents. We need someone who can help the team navigate that uncertainty and turn ambitious ideas into products people actually use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work closely with design, engineering, and content throughout the product development process, using tools like Claude Code to prototype concepts. You’ll help shape what we build next, keep the team focused, and move projects from early ideation to launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own major product initiatives, from defining the problem through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with design and engineering from early exploration through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write product requirements, set priorities, and keep projects moving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate planning, reviews, and communication across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the team make informed decisions through user research, data, experiments, and using Co–Star deeply yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go deep on important product questions when needed, whether that means conducting user research, designing experiments, or working through a difficult tradeoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the team decide what matters most and make smart calls about quality, scope, and speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a hand in where the product goes next, not just how we get there.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You might be a fit if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re roughly 7+ years in, and you’ve spent that time building consumer software people love to use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know how to create structure without weighing a team down.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re as comfortable writing a spec as you are talking to users or reviewing a prototype.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can work from a half-formed idea and help it find its shape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a point of view, but care more about getting the product right than being right.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Claude Code and Cursor are part of your workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work &amp;gt; ego&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully covered $0 deductible healthcare + vision, dental, and therapy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) + 5% matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited vacation + 2-week company-wide recharge at the end of each year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equipment budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12 weeks 100% paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-time. New York preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation: 180k–220k + benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Have you made an Instagram carousel as part of your art or writing practice? Do you reference Simone Weil and &lt;em&gt;Sex and the City&lt;/em&gt; with equal weight? Are you bonded deeply with a sister, friend, cousin or mother who drinks out of a Stanley Cup? Conceptually, what astrological sign answers yes to all three of these questions?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are expanding our social media department creatively and in headcount. This role includes work on new branding projects as well.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To write for our social media and brand, we must be a responsive team that listens to the world’s cues, processes them with sensitivity, and turns out timely interpretations that thrill a Co-Star-specific spectrum of people who read their horoscope daily.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please have a lifetime of experience consuming the internet, media and references that make you feel seen in this world, and hold reverence for the basic, the branded and the popular.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concept funny, smart, ownable insights for astrological signs. Go for weird, but be able to pull back to test for different angles&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with and punch other creatives’ work live in meetings as well as collaborate with team on yours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mock up your ideas visually&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sharp sense of how the internet talks, pop culture narrative past, present and future, and how to respond with humor, insight, and astrological interpretation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of astrology isn’t necessary, but piercing insight into human behavior is, whether through academia, astrology, therapy, or a lifetime of careful observation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to address and incorporate feedback on writing and concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hit deadlines consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident knowledge of IG, X and TikTok communities appreciated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Google Docs and Figma a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote, but local to NYC preferred&lt;/li&gt;
